Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:28:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/71] Make compaction keep per-request outcomes and a
 verbatim assistant tail

Compaction used to delete every assistant message, so the model lost all
record of what it had already done for each request and re-did work. The
summarization prompt now emits one outcome line per numbered user request,
and the newest assistant answers are carried through verbatim: whole
request groups are selected newest-first in code, so the boundary is a
pure function of the history and the prompt prefix stays cache-hot.
Tool traffic, reasoning, and system messages never consume that budget.

Budgets are sized for the real cost target rather than the upstream
defaults: the auto-compact trigger drops to 80k, user messages get 12k
and the assistant tail 8k, leaving ~59k of runway per window.

The trigger measurement was also overstating the next request's input.
`last_token_usage.total_tokens` bills the reasoning a turn produced, but
turn-scoped reasoning is only resent while that turn is still running, so
once the turn ends that amount is discounted. Reasoning is accumulated
per turn and callers pass the turn they are about to sample for, which
keeps the mid-turn tool loop measured as-is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
